-- title:
--   p-saturation of integral rational endomorphisms (Deuring)
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, and let $X$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic (nonsingular with invertible discriminant). Write $\mathcal{R} =$ [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k X`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) for the subring of the ring of additive endomorphisms of the group of affine points of $X$ generated by the set `rationalHomSet k X X`, that is, by those additive endomorphisms $\alpha$ which are either zero or satisfy the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented` (given by a pair of rational expressions in the coordinates). Assume that every point $P$ of $X$ with $p \cdot P = 0$ is zero, i.e. that $X$ has trivial $p$-torsion over $k$. Let $\varphi \in \mathcal{R}$ and suppose there are integers $t, n$ with $\varphi^2 - t \cdot \varphi + n \cdot 1 = 0$ in $\mathcal{R}$, with $p \mid t$ and $p^2 \mid n$. The conclusion is that $\varphi$ is divisible by $p$ inside $\mathcal{R}$: there exists $\psi \in \mathcal{R}$ with $\varphi = p \cdot \psi$.
--
--   This is Deuring's local maximality statement at $p$ in the form of a saturation property: an element of the ring of rational endomorphisms satisfying a monic integral quadratic relation with $p \mid t$, $p^2 \mid n$ already lies in $p$ times that ring. It feeds the construction of an isomorphism between the rational endomorphism ring of a supersingular curve and a maximal order in a definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $p$ and $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_eq_char_smul_of_sq_sub_smul_add_smul_eq_zero_rationalEndSubring.lean

